From b9259f3cf99b872417b366d2e8c8217b0edab5c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravi <ravi@openloopagentics.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:29:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] Support more than two layers, switched from a button

The daemon had exactly two layers, both bound to the Fn key: held Fn showed
layer 1, releasing returned to layer 0. There was no way to reach a third set
of buttons at all.

Make `layers` a Vec and add an [ExtraLayers] table of named layers, plus a
`Layer` key on a button that switches to one by name ("primary", "media", or
any extra) instead of sending keys:

  [ExtraLayers]
  fkeys = [ { Text = "F1", Action = "F1" }, ...,
            { Text = "back", Layer = "primary" } ]

Indices 0 and 1 keep the existing Fn behaviour, so Fn remains a guaranteed way
out of an extra layer even if its own back button is misconfigured. Extra
layers are sorted by name for stable indices across config reloads, and the
switch happens on touch-down while the touch stays bound to the layer it
started on, so the matching up-event still releases the right button.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
